meta {
  name: by-id
  seq: 9
}

auth {
  mode: inherit
}

docs {
  # Get-by-id tests (ONEROSTER-91)

  Covers `GET /{resource}/{id}` on all 12 rostering endpoints with the full-scope
  LEA token (`lea-odsApiToken`):

  - **valid id**: for each endpoint, take the first record of the collection
    (`?limit=1`) and fetch it by its `sourcedId`. Expect HTTP 200, a body with only
    the spec wrapper key (e.g. `class`, `user`, `demographics`) holding a single
    object, and the same record the collection returned.
  - **unknown id**: a well-formed id that matches nothing returns HTTP 404 in the
    `imsx_*` envelope, with no record.
  - **wrong sub-type**: a filtered endpoint doesn't return a record of another
    type, e.g. `/students/{id}` with a teacher's id returns 404. Covers terms and
    gradingPeriods (with a semester id), schools (district id), students (teacher
    id) and teachers (student id).

  The E2E data sets (Grand Bend) have no terms or grading periods: their sessions
  all map to `semester`. When `/terms` or `/gradingPeriods` is empty, its valid-id
  check is reported as `→ skipped, no terms in this data set` instead of failing.
  Every other collection must have at least one record.

  The single request runs `runByIdChecks` from `lib/by-id.js`, which reports each
  check as its own named test, e.g. `by-id › classes/{id} → 200`. The wrapper keys
  are in `lib/by-id.js`; the collection keys come from `lib/access-matrix.js`.
}
